I ran today's pipeline (Sunday, 2026-10-18) start to finish. It ended at **`awaiting_human_review`**, and GPT cross-verification passed on the first attempt with 0 issues.

- **Paper:** *To Stop or Not to Stop: Exploring the Intention-Behavior Gaps in Smartphone Usage* (Zheng & Choe), https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.08909. I read the full text. I looked at 12 candidates; the runner-up was the app activity log study (2609.24477).
- **What the study did:** 37 US Android users who wanted to cut back on phone use were asked mid-use, for at least two weeks, "I should ___ using my phone now" (1 = stop, 10 = continue). The app logged how long they kept going until they locked the screen.
- **Main number on the cards:** in 14.9% of the 5,772 responses, people answered on the "stop" side and still used the phone for more than 5 more minutes. That is a bit over half of all "stop" answers. The 14.9% counts moments, not people, and slide 4 says so.
- **Night finding:** at night, answers leaned more toward "stop", but once other factors are accounted for, people did not lock the screen noticeably earlier. I recorded that as a non-significant result, so the cards never say "people used it longer at night".
- **Visual:** the object is the stop–continue slider the study itself used, in accent color `#3D7A45`.
- **Self-check:** passed with 0 errors and 0 warnings.
- **Output check:** I opened all six final PNGs; nothing is cut off or overlapping.
- **Bookkeeping:** I added one line to `state/index.jsonl` and wrote `NOTES.md`.

Things to check before posting (all in `NOTES.md`):
1. **Publication status is unconfirmed.** The paper says it is published in PACMHCI (MobileHCI 2026), but its DOI (10.1145/3821659) returned 404 this morning and isn't registered yet. I didn't label it a preprint. Instead the caption says the official DOI page isn't open yet and the arXiv version was checked. If the DOI never resolves, switch the caption to the standard preprint notice.
2. **"A bit over half" is my own calculation** (14.9% ÷ 28.3%). The paper doesn't state it directly.
3. **Topic overlap:** the 10-09 (infinite-scroll stop prompts) and 09-27 (notification blocking) posts are also about stopping phone use. You may want to space them apart when scheduling.

Everything is in `output/20261018_그만_쓸까_물었을_때와_실제_사용/`.
